ges to $0$\n\n- if $|r|>1,$ the sequence is divergent\n\nMoreover, we have the following edge cases:\n\n- if $r=1,$ the sequence is convergent and converges to ${a}_{1}$\n\n- if $r=-1,$ the sequence is divergent\n\nFirst, we rewrite the sequence in the form ${a}_{n}=a\\cdot {r}^{n},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & =\\frac{4{(-7)}^{n}}{{2}^{n}} \\\\  & =4\\cdot \\frac{{(-7)}^{n}}{{2}^{n}} \\\\  & =4{(-\\frac{7}{2})}^{n}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now see that this is the geometric sequence with $r=-\\frac{7}{2}.$ \n\nSince $|r|>1,$ the sequence diverges." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-141312/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c023b634-e106-5fbc-a8ff-197f3aa4869d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-141312"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-351615/field-1/b785f042bcb1e3ac9f1c15e72aea8c54b522212617bb84e48c5ba505bb17b3ea" :answer/id #uuid "ee4257dd-8fdf-53c3-a5ab-baf7a45024d1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\ge" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-351615/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "9e3a2a2f-40d4-555b-be1f-fc48eb722dfe" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-351615/field-1/b785f042bcb1e3ac9f1c15e72aea8c54b522212617bb84e48c5ba505bb17b3ea" :answer-field/choices ["q-351615/field-1/b785f042bcb1e3ac9f1c15e72aea8c54b522212617bb84e48c5ba505bb17b3ea"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-351615/field-2/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "f0a72860-a954-5dc9-9b7a-69f590e80408" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-351615/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "2980df56-78e6-5c31-803e-dd233a57b872" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-351615/field-2/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer-field/choices ["q-351615/field-2/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-351615" :question/id #uuid "3132db17-2a7c-561c-a962-a110c8710c4d" :question/math-academy-id "q-351615" :question/problem "Consider the geometric sequence ${a}_{n}=12{(\\frac{4}{{x}^{2}})}^{n},$ where $x$ is a positive real number and $n\\ge 1.$ Find the values of $x$ for which the sequence converges.\n\n$x$\n\n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have a geometric sequence with the first term ${a}_{1}$ and common ratio $r.$ Then, we have the following convergence properties:\n\n- if $|r|<1,$ the sequence is convergent and converges to $0$\n\n- if $|r|>1,$ the sequence is divergent\n\nMoreover, we have the following edge cases:\n\n- if $r=1,$ the sequence is convergent and converges to ${a}_{1}$\n\n- if $r=-1,$ the sequence is divergent\n\nThe given sequence is a geometric sequence with the common ratio $r=\\frac{4}{{x}^{2}}.$ \nSince ${x}^{2}$ is positive,  $r$ is also positive, So, the convergence condition is $0<r\\le 1.$ \n\nTherefore, the  sequence converges for \n\n$$\n0<\\frac{4}{{x}^{2}}\\le 1\\,⟹\\,{x}^{2}\\ge 4.\n$$\n\nTaking into account the fact that $x$ is positive, we get\n\n$$\nx\\ge 2.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-351615/field-1" "q-351615/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "126485fb-1b7f-5602-bc8d-05908ac6f37c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-351615"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-141323/selection/b4e8fd139f2ef29e99838a47bc297c595fb8a4008594ca241c807dd55562633d" :answer/id #uuid "a566fd21-f4f0-5952-9dea-d1071f8e28b5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\ge \\frac{1}{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141323/selection/3cfc233d457edbec6b6deb35df070179afd90e6508c5585cd03e094cf600a715" :answer/id #uuid "72339277-a4ca-5cf4-9a53-9bbb934d0e0d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\ge 1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141323/selection/c5bb8c11b7ecd47cf5ad74fbbe08be4c380eec924210970be192c7c21423380d" :answer/id #uuid "47b01622-9184-5fa3-b41e-d61bd69a85c8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\ge 8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141323/selection/eb974af25f7cad614022cdd558a4e8472f5e3e606b024c17f3db85b309d0ab74" :answer/id #uuid "ee670c7b-0721-5856-879d-022ed9bf236c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0<x\\le 1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141323/selection/ae89af22804c27cea79f8976f240947aab92720967d9190be82a224bd96c5aea" :answer/id #uuid "f3071869-b2f6-5a56-8be8-7b60f0fe4139" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0<x\\le 8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141323/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "5f00b020-81e5-5940-bfc3-9a677aa0424b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-141323/selection/c5bb8c11b7ecd47cf5ad74fbbe08be4c380eec924210970be192c7c21423380d" :answer-field/choices ["q-141323/selection/b4e8fd139f2ef29e99838a47bc297c595fb8a4008594ca241c807dd55562633d" "q-141323/selection/3cfc233d457edbec6b6deb35df070179afd90e6508c5585cd03e094cf600a715" "q-141323/selection/c5bb8c11b7ecd47cf5ad74fbbe08be4c380eec924210970be192c7c21423380d" "q-141323/selection/eb974af25f7cad614022cdd558a4e8472f5e3e606b024c17f3db85b309d0ab74" "q-141323/selection/ae89af22804c27cea79f8976f240947aab92720967d9190be82a224bd96c5aea"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-141323" :question/id #uuid "1ecf569a-17ef-54e4-9a64-9ec3bdecb9da" :question/math-academy-id "q-141323" :question/problem "Consider the geometric sequence ${a}_{n}=\\frac{x}{4}{(\\frac{8}{x})}^{n},$ where $x$ is a positive real number and $n\\ge 1.$ What are the values of $x$ for which the sequence converges?" :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have a geometric sequence with the first term ${a}_{1}$ and common ratio $r.$ Then, we have the following convergence properties:\n\n- if $|r|<1,$ the sequence is convergent and converges to $0$\n\n- if $|r|>1,$ the sequence is divergent\n\nMoreover, we have the following edge cases:\n\n- if $r=1,$ the sequence is convergent and converges to ${a}_{1}$\n\n- if $r=-1,$ the sequence is divergent\n\nThe given sequence is a geometric sequence with the common ratio $r=\\frac{8}{x}.$ \nSince $x$ is positive,  $r$ is also positive, So, the convergence condition is $0<r\\le 1.$ \n\nTherefore, the  sequence converges for \n\n$$\n0<\\frac{8}{x}\\le 1\\,⟹\\,x\\ge 8.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-141323/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "126485fb-1b7f-5602-bc8d-05908ac6f37c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-141323"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-351612/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "995c8408-eabb-5584-8c05-afb7cfc4d9fe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-351612/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "cb6f2b7c-47fc-59a2-abdc-f088694d4b56" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-351612/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer-field/choices ["q-351612/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-351612/field-2/f022eff7ecaa4435243255d76a2a932e99db9e71ca2b89b05fafca75800709a0" :answer/id #uuid "d395a9f6-0343-5086-b068-3f378b188f62" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\le" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-351612/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "f8287ae1-9e32-5922-86f0-37098b44100e" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-351612/field-2/f022eff7ecaa4435243255d76a2a932e99db9e71ca2b89b05fafca758