-solution "Suppose we have a geometric sequence with the first term ${a}_{1}$ and common ratio $r.$ Then, we have the following convergence properties:\n\n- if $|r|<1,$ the sequence is convergent and converges to $0$\n\n- if $|r|>1,$ the sequence is divergent\n\nMoreover, we have the following edge cases:\n\n- if $r=1,$ the sequence is convergent and converges to ${a}_{1}$\n\n- if $r=-1,$ the sequence is divergent\n\nThe given sequence is a geometric sequence with the common ratio $r=2x.$ \nSince $x$ is positive,  $r$ is also positive, So, the convergence condition is $0<r\\le 1.$ \n\nTherefore, the  sequence converges for \n\n$$\n0<2x\\le 1\\,⟹\\,0<x\\le \\frac{1}{2}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-141318/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "126485fb-1b7f-5602-bc8d-05908ac6f37c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-141318"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-74633/selection/98ff92445dc92a3eb402958e5d5f65f0c86bfcc7d7b2c116ada1e99a96b1c47d" :answer/id #uuid "a8537119-574a-5f8a-9df6-e74b7f9e6bd5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0<x\\le 4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74633/selection/1235061e5472926481ddeb36b23313e44d3189b3ae0ecc652c6bbec56a95bfe7" :answer/id #uuid "f47ee072-c12d-508a-98e0-716d0a8e52e8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x>2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74633/selection/6f27755cbecd36cf5ed6b27aef81baa95f913bc664277798c75f0df67ef658ac" :answer/id #uuid "58d775e7-38de-5a1d-898b-33b5dab186c6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0<x<2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74633/selection/8f9d5e78c71265e01c3fb8d0d07a71e7cb16e44cf95a17717304ef60938a6591" :answer/id #uuid "8e4e8e39-e893-5354-b663-09ac379deecb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\ge 4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74633/selection/ebe6f4d26afa362a416b64d63b5c4b51d9e2ae71005bcb2b10a9632f19911f50" :answer/id #uuid "5e4fc8ea-769c-56d3-94e8-d87f2544c172" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\ge 2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74633/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "52b8db26-97d0-5544-b6e5-d7e0671f2706" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-74633/selection/ebe6f4d26afa362a416b64d63b5c4b51d9e2ae71005bcb2b10a9632f19911f50" :answer-field/choices ["q-74633/selection/98ff92445dc92a3eb402958e5d5f65f0c86bfcc7d7b2c116ada1e99a96b1c47d" "q-74633/selection/1235061e5472926481ddeb36b23313e44d3189b3ae0ecc652c6bbec56a95bfe7" "q-74633/selection/6f27755cbecd36cf5ed6b27aef81baa95f913bc664277798c75f0df67ef658ac" "q-74633/selection/8f9d5e78c71265e01c3fb8d0d07a71e7cb16e44cf95a17717304ef60938a6591" "q-74633/selection/ebe6f4d26afa362a416b64d63b5c4b51d9e2ae71005bcb2b10a9632f19911f50"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-74633" :question/id #uuid "ccc82d1a-8b77-5855-b94b-af517ea6204a" :question/math-academy-id "q-74633" :question/problem "Consider the sequence ${a}_{n}=\\frac{{2}^{n+4}}{{x}^{n}},$ where $x$ is a positive real number and $n\\ge 1.$ What are the values of $x$ for which the sequence converges?" :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have a geometric sequence with the first term ${a}_{1}$ and common ratio $r.$ Then, we have the following convergence properties:\n\n- if $|r|<1,$ the sequence is convergent and converges to $0$\n\n- if $|r|>1,$ the sequence is divergent\n\nMoreover, we have the following edge cases:\n\n- if $r=1,$ the sequence is convergent and converges to ${a}_{1}$\n\n- if $r=-1,$ the sequence is divergent\n\nFirst, we rewrite the sequence in the form ${a}_{n}=a\\cdot {r}^{n},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & =\\frac{{2}^{n+4}}{{x}^{n}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{2}^{n}\\cdot {2}^{4}}{{x}^{n}} \\\\  & ={2}^{4}\\cdot \\frac{{2}^{n}}{{x}^{n}} \\\\  & =16{(\\frac{2}{x})}^{n}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nWe see that this is a geometric sequence with the common ratio $r=\\frac{2}{x}.$ Since $x$ is positive,  $r$ is also positive. So, the convergence condition is $0<r\\le 1.$ \n\nTherefore, the  sequence converges for \n\n$$\n0<\\frac{2}{x}\\le 1\\,⟹\\,x\\ge 2.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-74633/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "abad9fa9-b426-50aa-aaa7-d472ea974f98"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-74633"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-141336/selection/eb974af25f7cad614022cdd558a4e8472f5e3e606b024c17f3db85b309d0ab74" :answer/id #uuid "ef467f4e-409b-517a-aeec-b3fa016a3e16" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0<x\\le 1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141336/selection/ae89af22804c27cea79f8976f240947aab92720967d9190be82a224bd96c5aea" :answer/id #uuid "711c5c2d-64ad-5ec4-ac8c-7f03e42142e1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0<x\\le 8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141336/selection/98ff92445dc92a3eb402958e5d5f65f0c86bfcc7d7b2c116ada1e99a96b1c47d" :answer/id #uuid "8e9bcbd0-2e1b-554e-af72-46b48bd0521c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0<x\\le 4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141336/selection/8f9d5e78c71265e01c3fb8d0d07a71e7cb16e44cf95a17717304ef60938a6591" :answer/id #uuid "d84806e1-564d-5919-aaf4-135ae3357756" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\ge 4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141336/selection/c5bb8c11b7ecd47cf5ad74fbbe08be4c380eec924210970be192c7c21423380d" :answer/id #uuid "1f8e88a6-3dd8-5d92-93d2-bf1b0e7d0112" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\ge 8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141336/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "8ef9f971-5077-59e8-815a-0e5b8718a9d1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-141336/selection/98ff92445dc92a3eb402958e5d5f65f0c86bfcc7d7b2c116ada1e99a96b1c47d" :answer-field/choices ["q-141336/selection/eb974af25f7cad614022cdd558a4e8472f5e3e606b024c17f3db85b309d0ab74" "q-141336/selection/ae89af22804c27cea79f8976f240947aab92720967d9190be82a224bd96c5aea" "q-141336/selection/98ff92445dc92a3eb402958e5d5f65f0c86bfcc7d7b2c116ada1e99a96b1c47d" "q-141336/selection/8f9d5e78c71265e01c3fb8d0d07a71e7cb16e44cf95a17717304ef60938a6591" "q-141336/selection/c5bb8c11b7ecd47cf5ad74fbbe08be4c380eec924210970be192c7c21423380d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-141336" :question/id #uuid "c5a00789-960c-5600-b89b-62bbd0168b4a" :question/math-academy-id "q-141336" :question/problem "Consider the sequence ${a}_{n}=\\frac{{x}^{2n}}{{16}^{n+1}},$ where $x$ is a positive real number and $n\\ge 1.$ What are the values of $x$ for which the sequence converges?" :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have a geometric sequence with the first term ${a}_{1}$ and common ratio $r.$ Then, we have the following convergence properties:\n\n- if $|r|<1,$ the sequence is convergent and converges to $0$\n\n- if $|r|>1,$ the sequence is divergent\n\nMoreover, we have the following edge cases:\n\n- if $r=1,$ the sequence is convergent and converges to ${a}_{1}$\n\n- if $r=-1,$ the sequence is divergent\n\nFirst, we rewrite the sequence in the form ${a}_{n}=a\\cdot {r}^{n},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & =\\frac{{x}^{2n}}{{16}^{n+1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2n}}{16\\cdot {16}^{n}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{16}\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{2n}}{{16}^{n}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{16}\\cdot {(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{16})}^{n}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nWe see that this is a geometric sequence with the common ratio $r=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{16}.$ Since ${x}^{2}$ is positive, $r$ is also positive.  So, the convergence condition is $0<r\\le 1.$ \n\nTherefore, the  sequence converges for\n\n$$\n0<\\frac{{x}^{2}}{16}\\le 1\\,⟹\\,0<{x}^{2}\\le 16.\n$$\n\nTaking into account that $x$ is positive, we get\n\n$$\n0<x\\le 4.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-141336/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "abad9fa9-b426-50aa-aaa7-d472ea974f98"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-141336"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-351624/field-1/b785f042bcb1e3ac9f1c15e72aea8c54b522212617bb84e48c5ba505bb17b3ea" :answer/id #uuid "2741cff5-299e-52df-85d9-7c5cc30c09d8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\ge" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-351624/field-1/e4e9dbe71f63d8d81739fdcbf2df64ccccd4c8f5d299ddc4b1c1f96031adb38e" :answer/id #uuid "61918bf9-c6bb-51a1-b6c9-46f42e7f06d3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "<" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-351624/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "37c79175-7c41-5789-a713-e1c4d23f82ad" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-351624/field-1/b785f042bcb1e3ac9f1c15e72aea8c54b522212617bb84e48c5ba505bb17b3ea" :answer-field/choices ["q-351624/field-1/b785f042bcb1e3ac9f1c15e72aea8c54b522212617bb84e48c5ba505bb17b3ea" "q-351624/field-1/e4e9dbe71f63d8d81739fdcbf2df64ccccd4c8f5d299ddc4b1c1f96031adb38e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-351624/field-2/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "51928584-76c6-552c-9593-29a9eeb41693" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-351624/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "099d1a1b-b0db-583a-a75d-9fa2d2ffc314" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-351624/field-2/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer-field/choices ["q-351624/field-2/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-351624" :question/id #uuid "bbb4cb0e-6156-5433-b10c-c0559539044a" :question/math-academy-id "q-351624" :question/problem "Consider the sequence ${a}_{n}=\\frac{{x}^{4-n}}{{x}^{5n}},$ where $x$ is a positive real number and $n\\ge 1.$ Find the values of $x$ for which the sequence converges.\n\n$x$\n\n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have a geometric sequence with the first term ${a}_{1}$ and common ratio $r.$ Then, we have the following convergence properties:\n\n- if $|r|<1,$ the sequence is convergent and converges to $0$\n\n- if $|r|>1,$ the sequence is divergent\n\nMoreover, we have the following edge cases:\n\n- if $r=1,$ the sequence is convergent and converges to ${a}_{1}$\n\n- if $r=-1,$ the sequence is divergent\n\nFirst, we rewrite the sequence in the form ${a}_{n}=a\\cdot {r}^{n},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & =\\frac{{x}^{4-n}}{{x}^{5n}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{4}\\cdot {x}^{-n}}{{x}^{5n}} \\\\  & ={x}^{4}\\cdot \\frac{1}{{x}^{6n}} \\\\  & ={x}^{4}\\cdot {(\\frac{1}{{x}^{6}})}^{n}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nWe see that this is a geometric sequence with the common ratio $r=\\frac{1}{{x}^{6}}.$ Since ${x}^{6}$ is positive,  $r$ is also positive. So, the convergence condition is $0<r\\le 1.$ \n\nTherefore, the  sequence converges for \n\n$$\n0<\\frac{1}{{x}^{6}}\\le 1\\,⟹\\,{x}^{6}\\ge 1.\n$$\n\nTaking into account the fact that $x$ is positive, we get\n\n$$\nx\\ge 1.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-351624/field-1" "q-351624/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "abad9fa9-b426-50aa-aaa7-d472ea974f98"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-351624"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-123344/selection/c4d8fcc3d0001d305927fbe8d5a0bcc565b987d26bf192f936c7579b4dde886a" :answer/id #uuid "b2d21f04-20c5-5e88-898a-07eecd9e3fcb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x>0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123344/selection/eb974af25f7cad614022cdd558a4e8472f5e3e606b024c17f3db85b309d0ab74" :answer/id #uuid "85aadba4-72e1-562a-a0a9-f3856aaf1d09" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0<x\\le 1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123344/selec